      "round_summary": "Round 1/3 — Fix initialization read-before-write bug in `cubeAbs.scala`. Error: `current_pos_visited` assertion fails (dut_bug). Root cause: `visited(posReg) := true.B` on line 39 reads the **old** register value of `posReg` (0) instead of the newly computed value (15), because Chisel when-block assignments are concurrent. Fix: extract a combinational wire `initPos` before the `when` block and use it as the index into `visited` (line 39 changed to `visited(initPos) := true.B`), ensuring the visited array marks the correct initial position. The `current_pos_visited` assertion (line 71) is preserved verbatim. No homologous assertions found — the pattern `visited(dest) := true.B` in the `.otherwise` block uses `dest` which is already a combinational wire, so it is not affected by read-before-write semantics.",
