      "round_summary": "Round 2/3 — Fix combinational-sampling bug in `liveness_visit_unvisited` assertion (assertion_error). Root cause: `astRelaxedLiveness(initDone && !visited(dest), visited(dest), 5, ...)` used `dest` (a combinational wire changing every cycle) in both trigger and eventual conditions. The consequent `visited(dest)` checked the *current* combinational `dest` (always a different unvisited position) instead of the position that triggered the check, so the timer monotonically incremented every cycle until overflow at 5 cycles. Fix: replaced `astRelaxedLiveness` with a manual liveness checker (lines 84-103) that latches `dest` into `pending_dest` when the trigger fires (and no earlier check is pending), then checks `visited(pending_dest)` against a bounded timer. This ensures the consequent targets the same position that triggered the check. The assertion label `liveness_visit_unvisited` is preserved exactly. No homologous assertions found — this is the only `astRelaxedLiveness` call in the file.",
